#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:247
msgid "Is double precision enough for unit conversion?"
msgstr "¿Es suficiente la doble precisión para la conversión de unidades?"

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2282
msgid "Is ground speed the same as airspeed?"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2574
msgid "Is higher mpg always better than lower L/100 km?"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:928
msgid "Is Kelvin written with a degree symbol?"
msgstr "¿Kelvin se escribe con un símbolo de grado?"

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1225
msgid "Is SI always the right choice?"
msgstr "¿Es SI siempre la elección correcta?"

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:93
msgid "Is the metric system the same as SI?"
msgstr "¿El sistema métrico es lo mismo que SI?"

#: src/components/conversion-details.tsx:396
#: src/routes/$lang/convert.$quantity.$from.to.$to.tsx:88
msgid "Is this {tFrom} to {tTo} converter free?"
msgstr "¿Este convertidor de {tFrom} a {tTo} es gratuito?"

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:908
msgid "Isaac Newton experimented with a temperature scale based on freely cooling materials and other references. The Newton scale appears in some converters as a historical curiosity with a zero near freezing and a smaller degree count to boiling."
msgstr "Isaac Newton experimentó con una escala de temperatura basada en materiales que se enfriaban libremente y otras referencias. La escala de Newton aparece en algunos convertidores como una curiosidad histórica con un cero cercano al punto de congelación y un número menor de grados hasta el punto de ebullición."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1877
msgid "ISO-8601 durations (PT1H30M) encode units explicitly. When APIs return raw seconds, document that contract. Silent disagreement between “seconds since start” and “minutes since start” is a frequent integration bug."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1750
msgid "It depends on the country. In most of the world, highway “100” means 100 km/h (about 62 mph). In the United States, “100” would be mph if used—always read local unit conventions."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:398
msgid "It depends on which cup. A common modern US legal cup for nutrition labelling is 240 mL. A metric cup is often 250 mL. Check the recipe’s origin and prefer millilitre measurements when accuracy matters."
msgstr "Depende de qué taza. Una taza legal moderna común en los EE. UU. para el etiquetado nutricional es de 240 ml. Una taza métrica suele tener 250 ml. Verifique el origen de la receta y prefiera medidas en mililitros cuando la precisión sea importante."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2326
msgid "Jet lag feelings track circadian clocks, not unit converters. Still, computing elapsed awake time uses duration units: hours since last sleep, minutes of layover."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1793
msgid "Jet streams and ATIS winds are typically in knots. Airport visibility and runway lengths may use metres or feet—different quantities. Do not treat a wind of 15 kt like 15 km/h; that underestimates wind by nearly half."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1936
msgid "Julian calendar dates (the historical calendar Julius Caesar introduced) are yet another topic. “Julian year” as a 365.25-day unit should not be confused with Julian calendar day numbering or Julian Day Count (JD), though the shared adjective confuses newcomers."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1914
msgid "Julian Year vs Calendar Year"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2402
msgid "Keep a paper trail: density value + source + temperature, mass with unit, volume with unit, then the computed third quantity. Unitless triangles are how lab notebooks go wrong."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1510
msgid "Keep a pool data card"
msgstr "Mantenga una tarjeta de datos de la piscina"

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1731
msgid "Keep a single sticky note on the dash for the first day abroad: “limits are km/h” or “limits are mph,” plus two anchor conversions you actually saw on the route."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:383
msgid "Keep a small card on the fridge with your most-used pairs: cup ↔ mL, tablespoon ↔ mL, butter stick ↔ grams if relevant in your country. Habit beats hunting mid-batter."
msgstr "Guarde una pequeña tarjeta en el refrigerador con los pares más utilizados: taza ↔ ml, cucharada ↔ ml, barra de mantequilla ↔ gramos, si es relevante en su país. El hábito es mejor que cazar al medio bateador."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:467
msgid "Keep a small reference of the prefixes you actually use. You do not need yocto and yotta memorised for construction work; you do need milli, micro, and kilo cold. Add nano if you read materials or electronics papers; add mega and giga if you work with planetary or data-centre physical plant scales."
msgstr "Mantenga una pequeña referencia de los prefijos que realmente utiliza. No es necesario memorizar yocto y yotta para trabajos de construcción; necesitas mili, micro y kilo frío. Agregue nano si lee materiales o artículos sobre electrónica; agregue mega y giga si trabaja con escalas de plantas físicas planetarias o de centros de datos."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:976
msgid "Keep a tiny reference card: US gal ≈ 3.785 L; imperial gal ≈ 4.546 L; metric cup = 250 mL; US legal cup = 240 mL. Those four numbers prevent most kitchen disasters."
msgstr "Guarde una pequeña tarjeta de referencia: US gal ≈ 3,785 L; galones imperiales ≈ 4,546 L; taza métrica = 250 ml; Taza legal de EE. UU. = 240 ml. Esos cuatro números previenen la mayoría de los desastres en la cocina."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:152
msgid "Keep full precision through intermediate steps. Round once for the audience: a cooking blog may show one decimal place; a machine shop may need three. Rounding early in a multi-step calculation invents error that was not in the original measurement."
msgstr "Mantenga la precisión total a través de pasos intermedios. Ronda una vez para la audiencia: un blog de cocina puede mostrar un decimal; un taller mecánico puede necesitar tres. Redondear al principio de un cálculo de varios pasos inventa un error que no estaba en la medición original."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1183
msgid "Keep leading digits readable"
msgstr "Mantenga legibles los primeros dígitos"

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1455
msgid "Keep nautical miles separate for marine and aviation contexts—they are not the same as statute miles."
msgstr "Mantenga las millas náuticas separadas para contextos marítimos y de aviación; no son lo mismo que millas terrestres."

#: src/lib/units.ts:1186
msgid "Kelvin"
msgstr "Kelvin"

#: src/lib/units.ts:507
msgid "Kelvin (K) is the SI base unit of thermodynamic temperature. Absolute zero is 0 K; water's triple point is defined near 273.16 K."
msgstr "El kelvin (K) es la unidad base del SI de temperatura termodinámica. El cero absoluto es 0 K; el punto triple del agua se define cerca de 273,16 K."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:280
msgid "Kelvin anchors absolute zero at 0 K. The triple point of water and other defining fixed points connect Kelvin to laboratory practice. Scientists prefer Kelvin for equations of state, cryogenics, and colour temperature because ratios and absolute values behave cleanly."
msgstr "Kelvin fija el cero absoluto en 0 K. El punto triple del agua y otros puntos fijos definitorios conectan a Kelvin con la práctica de laboratorio. Los científicos prefieren Kelvin para las ecuaciones de estado, criogenia y temperatura de color porque las proporciones y los valores absolutos se comportan limpiamente."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:898
msgid "Kelvin and absolute temperature"
msgstr "Kelvin y temperatura absoluta"

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:295
msgid "Kelvin appears in physics, chemistry, astronomy, and lighting. Deep space backgrounds near 2.7 K, liquid nitrogen near 77 K, and steelmaking temperatures in the thousands of kelvin are easier to reason about without negative values."
msgstr "Kelvin aparece en física, química, astronomía e iluminación. Es más fácil razonar sobre fondos del espacio profundo cerca de 2,7 K, nitrógeno líquido cerca de 77 K y temperaturas de fabricación de acero en miles de kelvin sin valores negativos."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1388
msgid "Kelvin is rarely printed on consumer recipes but appears in science-of-cooking texts. Knowing that a 1 °C change equals a 1 K change helps when reading those charts."
msgstr "Kelvin rara vez aparece impreso en las recetas de los consumidores, pero aparece en textos sobre ciencia de la cocina. Saber que un cambio de 1 °C equivale a un cambio de 1 K ayuda a la hora de leer esos gráficos."

#: src/routes/$lang/about.tsx:80
msgid "Key Features"
msgstr "Características clave"

#: src/lib/units-mass-motion.ts:365
msgid "Kilogram"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1547
msgid "Kilograms and pounds both describe mass (weight under ordinary gravity). A suitcase that tips a scale at 23 kg is the same object whether a US tag says about 50.7 lb. The physics does not change; the number and the unit do. Confusion starts when people treat the numbers as interchangeable, round too early, or mix stone, pounds, and kilograms on one form."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1535
msgid "Kilograms vs Pounds in Everyday Life"
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/units.ts:1211
msgid "Kilometre"
msgstr "Kilómetro"

#: src/lib/units-mass-motion.ts:382
msgid "Kilometre per hour"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:522
msgid "Kilometres and miles outdoors"
msgstr "Kilómetros y millas al aire libre"

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2240
msgid "km/h, mph, and m/s in reports"
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/units-mass-motion.ts:385
msgid "Knot"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2232
msgid "Knots as the aviation default"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1760
msgid "Knots Explained for Boats and Planes"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:910
msgid "Knowing these scales exist helps when reading older papers—but for new work, prefer Celsius for communication and Kelvin for absolute thermodynamic quantities."
msgstr "Saber que existen estas escalas ayuda al leer artículos antiguos, pero para trabajos nuevos, prefiera Celsius para comunicación y Kelvin para cantidades termodinámicas absolutas."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2535
msgid "L/100 km ≈ (litres used × 100) / kilometres driven. km/L ≈ kilometres / litres. Those formulas only work after unit cleanup."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2567
msgid "Label every log line: distance unit, volume unit, economy style. Dual-display dashboards are fine; dual-meaning spreadsheets are not."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2192
msgid "Label every number: “72.1 kg (11 st 4 lb).” Dual labels prevent the 11.4 disaster."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2342
msgid "Label outputs: “duration 2 h 15 min” vs “09:00 JST.” Clear nouns prevent Slack threads from inventing physics."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:605
msgid "Labels, symbols, and UI pitfalls"
msgstr "Etiquetas, símbolos y errores de la interfaz de usuario"

#: src/lib/units.ts:1257
msgid "Lambda"
msgstr "Lambda"

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:78
msgid "Land and property use hectares and acres side by side in international markets. One hectare is 10 000 m²; one acre is 4 046.856 422 4 m² under the international definition. Real-estate listings sometimes round aggressively—verify the survey plat, not the marketing brochure."
msgstr "La tierra y la propiedad utilizan hectáreas y acres uno al lado del otro en los mercados internacionales. Una hectárea son 10.000 m²; un acre equivale a 4 046,856 422 4 m² según la definición internacional. Los listados de bienes raíces a veces son agresivos: verifique el plano de la encuesta, no el folleto de marketing."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:799
msgid "Land area units you will meet"
msgstr "Unidades de superficie terrestre que conocerás"

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:589
msgid "Land area versus water volume"
msgstr "Superficie terrestre versus volumen de agua"

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:443
msgid "Land metric units add hectare (10⁴ m²) and are (10² m²). They are accepted for use with SI even though they are not prefix forms of the metre. Still convert through square metres when mixing with square kilometres or acres."
msgstr "Las unidades métricas del suelo suman hectárea (10⁴ m²) y son (10² m²). Se acepta su uso con SI aunque no sean formas de prefijo del metro. Aún así, convierta en metros cuadrados cuando mezcle con kilómetros cuadrados o acres."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:790
msgid "Land-area conversion made clear: acres, hectares, square metres, and square kilometres—with exact factors and pitfalls from surveying history."
msgstr "La conversión de la superficie terrestre quedó clara: acres, hectáreas, metros cuadrados y kilómetros cuadrados, con factores exactos y dificultades de la historia topográfica."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1108
msgid "Landmarks from nanometre upward"
msgstr "Puntos de referencia desde el nanómetro hacia arriba"

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2019
msgid "Large commercial spaces sometimes mention acres for campuses, not for a single room. One acre is 4,046.8564224 m². Do not use acre converters for a bedroom—use m²/ft²."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2385
msgid "Large industrial batches may use metric tonnes (1 t = 1,000 kg) and cubic metres. Convert tonne → kg if your density table is in kg/m³."
msgstr ""

